1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,089
Verdict Picks Toon: A Warm Room for Grandma June

2
00:00:02,239 --> 00:00:06,114
The first snow of the year. Jo's grandmother lives alone.

3
00:00:06,264 --> 00:00:09,261
Don't fuss, dear. I have my old heater.

4
00:00:09,411 --> 00:00:12,652
Grandma... what is that heater plugged into?

5
00:00:12,802 --> 00:00:17,409
CPSC: never plug a space heater into an extension cord or a power strip.

6
00:00:17,559 --> 00:00:20,263
She's getting a new one. Tonight.

7
00:00:20,413 --> 00:00:24,385
Good call. One check before you buy any heater this winter.

8
00:00:24,535 --> 00:00:29,191
Find the model number on the label, then look it up in the recall notice.

9
00:00:29,341 --> 00:00:34,657
CPSC recall, October 29, 2026: Dreo DR-HSH015 (black, remote) recalled; Units in the US about 338,800; Hazard fire and burn Source: CPSC notice 27-054. The Dreo in our review is a different model; check yours against the notice.

10
00:00:34,807 --> 00:00:38,096
You drove all this way? You're worth the trip.

11
00:00:38,246 --> 00:00:43,292
Straight into the wall. Three feet clear of drapes, furniture and bedding (CPSC).

12
00:00:43,442 --> 00:00:48,390
Set it near 68°F. In Eco mode it stops heating once the room gets there (Dreo).

13
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:50,292
Warm at last.

14
00:00:50,442 --> 00:00:55,195
Off when you sleep or leave: CPSC and NFPA both say so. Goodnight, Grandma.

15
00:00:55,345 --> 00:00:57,846
Is the Dreo heater right for your room? Our full review is below. Link in description.

